D. TOPHRED33 / TOPHRED64 conversion:
   -phred33 input, TOPHRED64: output qualities read back with offset 64 equal the input integers for 200/200 reads
   -phred64 input, TOPHRED33: output read back with offset 33 equals the input for 200/200 reads
   -phred33 input, TOPHRED33: unchanged for 200/200 reads

E. automatic Phred-offset detection (no -phred flag; the parser histograms the first 10,000 reads):
   typical qualities (2-40) written Phred+33 -> ('Quality encoding detected as phred33', 0, 500)
   typical qualities (2-40) written Phred+64 -> ('Quality encoding detected as phred64', 0, 500)
